<title>FINLAND: OKOBANK'S OIP SETS FIM 100 MLN FIVE-YEAR BOND.</title>
<headline>OKOBANK'S OIP SETS FIM 100 MLN FIVE-YEAR BOND.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1996-09-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Finnish cooperative bank OKOBANK said in a statement on Monday its OKO-Investointipankki (OIP) was launching a 5.30 percent coupon five-year variable rate bond maturing on September 24, 2001.</p>
<p>Coupon payments would be yearly, it said.</p>
<p>The subsciption period will run from September 24, 1996  to January 24, 1997, after which the bond would be listed on the Helsinki Stock Exchange, OKOBANK said.</p>
<p>-- Helsinki newsroom +358-0-6805 0245</p>
